  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {κ c r₀ : ℝ} {η : ℕ → ℝ},\n  1 ≤ κ →\n    0 < c →\n      c < 1 / 4 →\n        0 ≤ r₀ →\n          (∀ (n : ℕ), 0 < η n ∧ η n ≤ c) →\n            have K := fun r => (1 + r) / (κ⁻¹ + r);\n            have τ := fun r => if 2 ≤ K r then K r else c;\n            have a := fun r h => (h + τ r) / (1 + r);\n            have step := fun r h => r + (a r h)⁻¹;\n            have r := fun t => Nat.rec r₀ (fun j r => step r (η j)) t;\n            (∀ (n : ℕ), 0 ≤ r n ∧ 0 < r (n + 1)) ∧\n              (Antitone fun n => K (r n)) ∧\n                (∀ (m n : ℕ), m ≤ n → K (r m) < 2 → K (r n) < 2) ∧\n                  (∀ (M N : ℕ),\n                      (4 / 5) ^ M * K r₀ < 2 →\n                        0 < (r (M + 1 + N))⁻¹ ∧ (r (M + 1 + N))⁻¹ ≤ 2 * c * (2 * c / (1 + 2 * c)) ^ N) ∧\n                    ∀ (B : ℝ), 0 < B → ∃ J, 0 < J ∧ 0 < (r J)⁻¹ ∧ (r J)⁻¹ ≤ B",
    "statement_sha256": "a4e9db522739a3eabd69ae52b3ae042423c2b32f730f08724af6ce828b0783c7",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "ℝ denotes the real numbers, ℕ the natural numbers starting at zero. Real reciprocal is totalized: 0⁻¹=0. A have-expression in a displayed type introduces a local abbreviation. Nat.rec z f defines the sequence with value z at zero and value f j (previous value) at j+1. Antitone f means that m≤n implies f n≤f m. All functions and operations are as explicitly defined in the displayed statement."
    ]
  },
